# Installation

## dotnet magic

```
dotnet new create blazorwasm -o AlmToo

dotnet publish -c Release -o publish AlmToo.csproj 
```


## Required Packages

apt update
apt install npm
apt install dotnet-sdk-10.0

npm install -g @github/copilot
npx @opengsd/gsd-core@latest
npx @opengsd/gsd-pi@latest

## Verified browser-local workflow

The clone, browse, edit, save, changed-file review, and local commit flow has been
verified with the small public repository
`https://github.com/octocat/Hello-World.git`.

Current limitations:

- repositories must be publicly readable over HTTPS for clone/open;
- repository data, local commits, and Git-Bug issue edits/comments remain in browser-local storage until explicitly published;
- central publication is limited to the reviewed Git-Bug refs and required identity ref from the active repository, through the explicit review, credential, confirmation, and push flow;
- credentials are tab-scoped, are not stored in repository configuration, and are cleared after publication or a rejected/failed publication attempt;
- remote-ahead, credential rejection, network loss, unsupported refs, and stale reviews require explicit recovery and are never retried implicitly;
- the M013 acceptance proof uses a disposable controlled smart-HTTP remote; arbitrary hosted remotes, issue closing, pull/reconciliation, bridge management, and hosted issue synchronization remain outside this product boundary;
- browser storage capacity and Git object traversal are the practical repository-size limits, so small interactive repositories are recommended.

